"source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "Assessments": {"value": "", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "ImageDescription": {"value": "North Cape is on the northern coast of the island of Magerøya in Northern Norway and happens to be the northernmost point on the European mainland. The cliffs in this area are a formidable meeting place for countless species of seabirds to feed, nest and breed. It is home to some of the most beautiful colonies of species, such as Atlantic puffin (Fratercula arctica). One of the Copernicus Sentinel-2 satellites acquired this rare cloudless image of North Cape on 22 May 2022.", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "DateTimeOriginal": {"value": "2022-05-22", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Credit": {"value": "<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.copernicus.eu/en/media/image-day-gallery/norway-north-cape\">https://www.copernicus.eu/en/media/image-day-gallery/norway-north-cape</a>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Artist": {"value": "European Union, Copernicus Sentinel-2 imagery", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "LicenseShortName": {"value": "Attribution", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "Attribution": {"value": "Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data 2022", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "Restrictions": {"value": "", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}}}]}]}}